THE SMOKE BREAK · PART 1 OF 2 · FORMAT & REFERENCES
FORMAT: same duration and aspect ratio as @Video 1 / two-lead replacement / one continuous handheld shot, keep original timing

REFERENCES:
@Video 1 is the camera, timing, composition and motion-capture master. It is uploaded muted. Treat it as a motion-capture track. It contains two LEADS: the LEAD IN THE WHITE NIKE TRACK JACKET — the black cat who dances, lights the cigarette, opens the jacket and blows out the smoke — and the OPENER IN THE LIGHT BLUE PUFFER VEST — the orange-and-white cat who dances at the very start. Each new lead's body follows the lead it replaces pose-for-pose, frame by frame: the same head position in frame, the same shoulder line, the same elbow angle, the same hand position, the same knee bend and foot placement, at the exact same moment, speed and direction. Keep everything else exactly as it is: the same continuous handheld camera move, framing and distance, the same rooftop with its metal railing, chimneys and tiled edges, the same city view at dusk, the same people around them and everything they do, the same light, grain and color grading. Do not inherit the two original cats' heads, fur, eyes or paws.

@Image 1 defines ONLY the new LEAD IN THE WHITE NIKE TRACK JACKET. It can be a person, a cat, a dog or any animal. Preserve this subject's face, eyes, eye condition, hair or fur color, fur pattern, ear shape, nose, skin or fur texture and any unique features — a different or cloudy eye, a scar, a mole, a missing ear tip, special markings — exactly as shown in @Image 1. Do not inherit the background, floor, furniture, lighting or clothes from @Image 1.
[optional: short description of your lead, and any unique feature with its exact side, e.g. "black cat, the cat's LEFT eye is cloudy and blind"]

@Image 2 defines ONLY the new OPENER IN THE LIGHT BLUE PUFFER VEST. It can be a person, a cat, a dog or any animal. Preserve this subject's face, eyes, eye condition, hair or fur color, fur pattern, ear shape, nose, skin or fur texture and any unique features exactly as shown in @Image 2. Do not inherit the background, floor, furniture, lighting or clothes from @Image 2.
[optional: short description of your opener, and any unique feature with its exact side]
